The examples in this directory are NOT described in the userguide.

Examples solve the height function equation

   dH      dH      dH
   -- + ux -- + uy -- = uz  
   dt      dx      dy

on a square domain and compare against the analytical manufactured solution

   H(x,y,t) = sin(2x+y-t)

with

   ux = sin(2x+y-t) + 2
   uy = 1
   uz = sin[2(2x+y-t)] + 4cos(2x+y-t)


Short description
-----------------

surface_advection1: 

 Test problem for the surface advection add-on (generic routine)
 An analytical solution on a 2D mesh (3D velocity vector) is tested.
 First-order time integration.

surface_advection2: 

 Test problem for the surface advection add-on (generic routine)
 An analytical solution on a 2D mesh (3D velocity vector) is tested.
 Second-order time integration.

surface_advection3: 

 Test problem for the surface advection add-on (generic routine)
 An analytical solution on a 2D mesh (3D velocity vector) is tested.
 Second-order time integration. First time step first-order.

